    '|a||And Bernoulli''s fix can be broken. In 1934 Karl Menger showed that prizes growing fast enough make even his utility add up to infinity again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1pu4adm'
    '|b||To block every such game, utility needs a ceiling: past some point, more money adds almost nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:10srvl0'
    '|a||Older answers exist too. In 1777 Buffon argued that a chance below about one in ten thousand is, in practice, zero.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15g0qar'
    '|a||How sure are we? That money matters less the more you have: mostly agreed. That utility alone solves the paradox: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1unbt2j'
    '|a||So how do you choose when the future is uncertain? Weigh each outcome by its chance, but by what it would mean to you, not by its dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1h9rpqa'
    '|a||Two new cases. Mia has $1,000 in savings. She can take a sure $1,000, or flip a coin for $2,200 or nothing. What does Bernoulli''s rule say?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:2tn67t'
    '|a||The sure $1,000: with her savings it doubles her wealth for certain, and the flip''s extra hundred on average can''t make up for the risk of getting nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A charity raffles a $50,000 car: tickets cost $10, and each has a 1-in-10,000 chance. What is a ticket''s expected value?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||$5: fifty thousand dollars times one in ten thousand. The other $5 is a gift to the charity.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Which leaves a puzzle. If a sure thing is worth more than a gamble with the same average, why do so many people buy both insurance and lottery tickets?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Yes: more, not less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Further up: the game is worth more to a millionaire, not less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||The flip''s average is higher, but missing out hurts her more than the extra $1,200 would help: here, the sure $1,000.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Multiply the prize by its chance, $50,000 × 1/10,000: here, $5.':
